IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tda-common`
IMPORT `fhog-terms`

-- First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (Tas) Part 2, with ss 20, 21 and 38, and the First Home Owner Grant Regulations 2021
-- regs 4, 5 and 5A. SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE, in the Act's terms ("the applicant", "the Commissioner", "an interested
-- person"); the questions are in tda-seat.l4. The Act and its Regulations are encoded here, beside the Duties Act,
-- because the two Acts are tied (NOTES.md); there is no encoding in their own folders.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 7 (entitlement; one grant per transaction; none after the HomeBuilder grant), ss 8-12 (criteria
-- 1-5), s 13 (eligible transaction, commencement date, completion, consideration), s 14(5)-(6) (the application
-- period), s 15 with regs 4, 5, 5A (who must join), s 18 with ss 18D-18M (the amount, as a dated table), s 19(3) (the
-- grant applied to State taxes), s 20 (payment in anticipation of the residence requirement: notice and repayment within
-- 14 days; regulative), s 21(3) (joint applicants), s 38 (repayment notice and penalty; regulative). Duties Act s 46X(2)
-- (no grant where the Division 2C concession was applied) is honoured as a fact.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: ss 18A-18C (1 January 2013 to 31 December 2015, for new homes: `not covered`); s 18 as it stood before
-- 1 January 2013 (`not covered`); the anticipatory top-ups in ss 18L(5) and 18M(5); s 13(6) moveable buildings
-- (`not covered`); s 16 (guardians), s 17(2) (payment before completion), s 22 (death), s 23 (correction, except as
-- the trigger for s 38), ss 25-29 (objections and appeals), Parts 3-4 other than ss 20, 21 and 38.
--
-- Edition: consolidation published 2026-10-14 (current 2026-10-20), deposited at
-- ../../../first-home-owner-grant-act-2000/registers/source-bundle/act-2000-019.txt; Regulations consolidation published
-- 2026-06-11, deposited at ../../../first-home-owner-grant-regulations-2021/registers/source-bundle/sr-2021-033.txt.
-- Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 20 October 2026 (State of Tasmania, CC BY 4.0).
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 Part 2 -- the grant (seat-neutral core)`

§§ `Division 2 -- the eligibility criteria (ss 8-12)`

-- One applicant's facts. "spouse" is the FHOG Act's (s 6, fhog-terms.l4); "relevant interest" and "residential
-- property" likewise.
DECLARE `Grant applicant` HAS
    `is a natural person`                                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `age`                                                                                        IS A NUMBER
    `the Commissioner exempts the age requirement (s 8(2))`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an Australian citizen or a permanent resident`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant or spouse was a party to an earlier application, under this Act or a corresponding law, on which a grant was paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that earlier grant was paid back`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant or spouse held a relevant interest in residential property in Australia before 1 July 2000` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant or spouse, before the commencement date, held a relevant interest in residential property in Australia and occupied it as a residence for a continuous 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Criterion 5 (s 12): at application the Commissioner may pay in anticipation if satisfied of the intention (s 20(1)).
    `intends to meet, or has met, the residence requirement`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner exempts the applicant from the residence requirement (s 12(2))`            IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Criterion not met` IS ONE OF
    `criterion 1: an applicant is not a natural person aged at least 18 (s 8)`
    `criterion 2: no applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident (s 9)`
    `criterion 3: an applicant or spouse was paid an earlier grant and did not pay it back (s 10)`
    `criterion 4: an applicant or spouse held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000 (s 11(1))`
    `criterion 4: an applicant or spouse held and lived in residential property for 6 months before (s 11(3))`
    `criterion 5: an applicant will not meet the residence requirement and is not exempted (s 12)`

-- s 8(1): "An applicant ... must be -- (a) a natural person; and (b) at least 18 years of age." (2): the Commissioner may
-- exempt from (1)(b).
-- s 9: "(1) ... must be an Australian citizen or a permanent resident. (2) If an application is made by joint applicants
-- and one of the applicants is an Australian citizen or a permanent resident, it is not necessary for the other or
-- others to be".
-- s 10: "(1) ... an applicant is ineligible if -- (a) the applicant or the applicant's spouse has been a party to an
-- earlier application under this Act or a corresponding law; and (b) a grant was paid on the application. (2) An
-- applicant is not ineligible if the grant was paid but later paid back."
-- s 11: "(1) An applicant is ineligible if the applicant or the applicant's spouse has, before 1 July 2000, held -- (a)
-- a relevant interest in residential property in Tasmania; or (b) [a corresponding interest] in another State or a
-- Territory ... (3) An applicant is also ineligible if the applicant or the applicant's spouse has, at any time before
-- the commencement date of the eligible transaction ... -- (a) held a relevant interest in residential property ...; and
-- (b) occupied the property as a place of residence for a continuous period of at least 6 months."
-- s 12(1): the residence requirement; (2): the Commissioner may exempt a joint applicant if "(a) the applicant is one of
-- 2 or more joint applicants ...; and (b) at least one of the applicants complies with the residence requirement; and
-- (c) there are, in the Commissioner's opinion, good reasons".
GIVEN `a` IS A `Grant applicant`
      `a co-applicant is a citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a co-applicant meets the residence requirement`    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Criterion not met`
`the first criterion not met by` `a` `a co-applicant is a citizen or permanent resident` `a co-applicant meets the residence requirement` MEANS
    IF     (NOT `a`'s `is a natural person`)
        OR (    `a`'s `age` LESS THAN 18
            AND (NOT `a`'s `the Commissioner exempts the age requirement (s 8(2))`))
    THEN JUST `criterion 1: an applicant is not a natural person aged at least 18 (s 8)`
    ELSE IF     (NOT `a`'s `is an Australian citizen or a permanent resident`)
            AND (NOT `a co-applicant is a citizen or permanent resident`)
         THEN JUST `criterion 2: no applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident (s 9)`
         ELSE IF     `a`'s `the applicant or spouse was a party to an earlier application, under this Act or a corresponding law, on which a grant was paid`
                 AND (NOT `a`'s `that earlier grant was paid back`)
              THEN JUST `criterion 3: an applicant or spouse was paid an earlier grant and did not pay it back (s 10)`
              ELSE IF `a`'s `the applicant or spouse held a relevant interest in residential property in Australia before 1 July 2000`
                   THEN JUST `criterion 4: an applicant or spouse held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000 (s 11(1))`
                   ELSE IF `a`'s `the applicant or spouse, before the commencement date, held a relevant interest in residential property in Australia and occupied it as a residence for a continuous 6 months`
                        THEN JUST `criterion 4: an applicant or spouse held and lived in residential property for 6 months before (s 11(3))`
                        ELSE IF     (NOT `a`'s `intends to meet, or has met, the residence requirement`)
                                AND (NOT (    `a`'s `the Commissioner exempts the applicant from the residence requirement (s 12(2))`
                                          AND `a co-applicant meets the residence requirement`))
                             THEN JUST `criterion 5: an applicant will not meet the residence requirement and is not exempted (s 12)`
                             ELSE NOTHING

-- s 7(1)(a): "the applicant or, if there are 2 or more of them, each of the applicants complies with the eligibility
-- criteria". The first criterion not met by any applicant, in the order of the list.
GIVEN `all applicants` IS A LIST OF `Grant applicant`
      `rest`           IS A LIST OF `Grant applicant`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Criterion not met`
`the first criterion not met among` `all applicants` `rest` MEANS
    CONSIDER `rest`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a` FOLLOWED BY `others` THEN
        CONSIDER `the first criterion not met by` `a` `a citizen is among them` `a resident is among them`
        WHEN JUST `c` THEN JUST `c`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `the first criterion not met among` `all applicants` `others`
    WHERE
        `a citizen is among them` MEANS
                count `all applicants` GREATER THAN 1
            AND any (GIVEN `x` YIELD `x`'s `is an Australian citizen or a permanent resident`) `all applicants`
        `a resident is among them` MEANS
                count `all applicants` GREATER THAN 1
            AND any (GIVEN `x` YIELD `x`'s `intends to meet, or has met, the residence requirement`) `all applicants`

GIVEN `applicants` IS A LIST OF `Grant applicant`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Criterion not met`
`the eligibility criteria not met by` MEANS
    `the first criterion not met among` `applicants` `applicants`

§§ `Division 3 -- s 13 eligible transaction`

-- s 13(1): "An eligible transaction is any of the following: (a) a contract made on or after 1 July 2000 and before
-- 1 July 2014 for the purchase of a home in the State; (ab) a contract made on or after 1 July 2000 for the purchase of a
-- new home in the State; (b) a comprehensive home building contract made on or after 1 July 2000 by the owner of land in
-- the State, or a person who will, on completion of the contract, be the owner of land in the State, to have a home built
-- on the land; (c) the building of a home in the State by an owner builder if the building work commences on or after
-- 1 July 2000." (3): not if the Commissioner is of the opinion it is part of a scheme to circumvent the Act.
-- (4): "The commencement date ... is -- (a) in the case of a contract, the date when the contract is made; or (b) [for an
-- owner builder] (i) the date when laying the foundations for the home commences; or (ii) another date the Commissioner
-- considers appropriate". (5): completed "(a) [for a purchase when] (i) the purchaser becomes entitled to possession of
-- the home under the contract; and (ii) [the steps to register the purchaser's title] have been taken; or (b) [for a
-- building contract or an owner builder] the building is ready for occupation as a place of residence". (7): the
-- consideration is the price, the total consideration for the building work, or the owner builder's actual costs
-- "(excluding any allowance for the owner builder's own labour)".
DECLARE `Grant transaction kind` IS ONE OF
    `a contract to buy a home`
    `a comprehensive home building contract`
    `building the home as an owner builder`
    `buying a moveable building to put on my land (s 13(6))`

DECLARE `Grant transaction` HAS
    `kind`                                                                                       IS A `Grant transaction kind`
    `the home`                                                                                   IS A `Building facts`
    `is in Tasmania`                                                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the commencement date`                                                                      IS A DATE
    `the completion date`                                                                        IS A DATE
    `has been completed`                                                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the consideration`                                                                          IS A NUMBER
    `the applicant is, or on completion will be, the owner of the land`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner is of the opinion it is part of a scheme to circumvent the Act (s 13(3))`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Tasmanian HomeBuilder grant was paid for it (s 7(4))`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Duties Act Division 2C pre-completion concession was applied to the transfer (Duties Act s 46X(2))` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner extended the time for completion (ss 18D(3)-18M(2))`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner considers it replaces an earlier transaction between substantially the same parties (ss 18D(4)-18M(3))` IS A BOOLEAN

`the first day for eligible transactions (s 13(1))` MEANS YMD 2000 7 1
`the day contracts for established homes stopped qualifying (s 13(1)(a))` MEANS YMD 2014 7 1

DECLARE `Transaction answer` IS ONE OF
    `an eligible transaction (s 13(1))`
    `not an eligible transaction: the home is not in Tasmania`
    `not an eligible transaction: it commenced before 1 July 2000`
    `not an eligible transaction: a contract made from 1 July 2014 must be for a new home (s 13(1)(ab))`
    `not an eligible transaction: what is bought or built is not a home (s 4)`
    `not an eligible transaction: the builder's client is not, and will not be, the owner of the land (s 13(1)(b))`
    `not an eligible transaction: the Commissioner is of the opinion it is part of a scheme (s 13(3))`
    `not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

GIVEN `t` IS A `Grant transaction`
GIVETH A `Transaction answer`
`the s 13 test for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `t`'s `kind`
    WHEN `buying a moveable building to put on my land (s 13(6))` THEN `not covered` `the grant is sought for a moveable building (s 13(6)): not encoded`
    OTHERWISE
        IF (NOT `t`'s `is in Tasmania`)
        THEN `not an eligible transaction: the home is not in Tasmania`
        ELSE IF `t`'s `the commencement date` `is before` `the first day for eligible transactions (s 13(1))`
             THEN `not an eligible transaction: it commenced before 1 July 2000`
             ELSE IF (NOT `is a home (FHOG Act s 4)` (`t`'s `the home`))
                  THEN `not an eligible transaction: what is bought or built is not a home (s 4)`
                  ELSE IF `t`'s `the Commissioner is of the opinion it is part of a scheme to circumvent the Act (s 13(3))`
                       THEN `not an eligible transaction: the Commissioner is of the opinion it is part of a scheme (s 13(3))`
                       ELSE CONSIDER `t`'s `kind`
                            WHEN `a contract to buy a home` THEN
                                IF     `t`'s `the commencement date` `is before` `the day contracts for established homes stopped qualifying (s 13(1)(a))`
                                    OR `is a new home (FHOG Act s 3)` (`t`'s `the home`)
                                THEN `an eligible transaction (s 13(1))`
                                ELSE `not an eligible transaction: a contract made from 1 July 2014 must be for a new home (s 13(1)(ab))`
                            WHEN `a comprehensive home building contract` THEN
                                IF `t`'s `the applicant is, or on completion will be, the owner of the land`
                                THEN `an eligible transaction (s 13(1))`
                                ELSE `not an eligible transaction: the builder's client is not, and will not be, the owner of the land (s 13(1)(b))`
                            OTHERWISE `an eligible transaction (s 13(1))`

GIVEN `a` IS A `Transaction answer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transaction is eligible` IF
    CONSIDER `a`
    WHEN `an eligible transaction (s 13(1))` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 15 and regs 4, 5, 5A -- who must join in the application`

-- s 15: "(1) All interested persons must be applicants. (2) An interested person is a person who is, or will be, on
-- completion of the eligible transaction to which the application relates, an owner of the relevant home except such a
-- person who is excluded from the application of this section under the regulations." Reg 4: where the Commissioner
-- recognises a non-conforming interest (s 5(4)), "the holder of a relevant interest in the land (other than the holder of
-- the non-conforming interest) is excluded". Reg 5: "Homes Tasmania is excluded". Reg 5A: "The Commonwealth and Housing
-- Australia are excluded ... in respect of any interest in land held by the Commonwealth, or Housing Australia, as a
-- result of a Help to Buy arrangement." (s 5(2A) already makes that interest no relevant interest: finding 11.)
DECLARE `Co-owner` IS ONE OF
    `a person who is, or on completion will be, an owner of the home`
    `Homes Tasmania (reg 5)`
    `the Commonwealth or Housing Australia under a Help to Buy arrangement (reg 5A, s 5(2A))`
    `another holder of a relevant interest, where the Commissioner recognised the applicant's non-conforming interest (reg 4)`

GIVEN `c` IS A `Co-owner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must join in the application (s 15)` IF
    CONSIDER `c`
    WHEN `a person who is, or on completion will be, an owner of the home` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 7 -- entitlement`

-- s 7(1): "A first home owner grant is payable on an application under this Act if -- (a) the applicant or, if there
-- are 2 or more of them, each of the applicants complies with the eligibility criteria; and (b) the transaction for
-- which the grant is sought -- (i) is an eligible transaction; and (ii) has been completed." (3): "Only one first home
-- owner grant is payable for the same eligible transaction." (4): not "if the Tasmanian HomeBuilder grant ... has been
-- paid in respect of the transaction". Duties Act s 46X(2): "If a duty concession is applied in respect of a transfer
-- under this Division [2C], a grant under the First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 is not payable in relation to the agreement
-- for sale". s 15: every interested person must be an applicant.
DECLARE `Entitlement answer` IS ONE OF
    `the grant is payable (s 7)`
    `not payable` HAS `because` IS A `Criterion not met`
    `not payable: the transaction is not eligible` HAS `because` IS A `Transaction answer`
    `not payable: the transaction has not been completed (s 7(1)(b)(ii))`
    `not payable: the HomeBuilder grant was paid (s 7(4))`
    `not payable: the Duties Act Division 2C concession was applied (Duties Act s 46X(2))`
    `not payable: an interested person has not joined in the application (s 15)`

GIVEN `applicants`  IS A LIST OF `Grant applicant`
      `t`           IS A `Grant transaction`
      `co-owners not applying` IS A LIST OF `Co-owner`
GIVETH AN `Entitlement answer`
`the s 7 entitlement` `applicants` `t` `co-owners not applying` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the transaction is eligible` (`the s 13 test for` `t`))
    THEN `not payable: the transaction is not eligible` (`the s 13 test for` `t`)
    ELSE CONSIDER `the eligibility criteria not met by` `applicants`
         WHEN JUST `c` THEN `not payable` `c`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
             IF any (GIVEN `c` YIELD `must join in the application (s 15)` `c`) `co-owners not applying`
             THEN `not payable: an interested person has not joined in the application (s 15)`
             ELSE IF (NOT `t`'s `has been completed`)
                  THEN `not payable: the transaction has not been completed (s 7(1)(b)(ii))`
                  ELSE IF `t`'s `the Tasmanian HomeBuilder grant was paid for it (s 7(4))`
                       THEN `not payable: the HomeBuilder grant was paid (s 7(4))`
                       ELSE IF `t`'s `the Duties Act Division 2C pre-completion concession was applied to the transfer (Duties Act s 46X(2))`
                            THEN `not payable: the Duties Act Division 2C concession was applied (Duties Act s 46X(2))`
                            ELSE `the grant is payable (s 7)`

GIVEN `a` IS AN `Entitlement answer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the grant is payable` IF
    CONSIDER `a`
    WHEN `the grant is payable (s 7)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 18 with ss 18D-18M -- the amount of the grant, as a dated table`

-- s 18(1): "The amount of a first home owner grant is the lesser of the following: (a) the consideration for the
-- eligible transaction; (b) the amount specified in subsection (2)." Note: "Where the consideration is zero, a grant is
-- not payable." (2): $15 000 if s 18A is satisfied, $30 000 for s 18B, $20 000 for each of ss 18C-18H, $30 000 for each
-- of ss 18I-18L, $20 000 for s 18M; "(b) if the first home owner grant relates to an eligible transaction that does not
-- satisfy section 18A, ... 18L or 18M, the amount is -- (i) if the eligible transaction commenced on or before 30 June
-- 2015, $7 000; and (ii) if the eligible transaction commenced on or after 1 July 2015, $10 000."
-- ss 18D-18M each: "An eligible transaction satisfies this section if -- (a) the commencement date of the eligible
-- transaction is on or after [from] but before [to]; and (b) the eligible transaction is completed in accordance with
-- section 13(5) within 24 months after the commencement date"; the Commissioner may extend the time to complete; and not
-- if the Commissioner considers the transaction "replaces a transaction, entered into before [from], ... between
-- substantially, or that benefits substantially, the same parties".
-- Periods (the last day is the day before "before"):
DECLARE `Grant period` HAS
    `section`                 IS A STRING
    `commencing on or after`  IS A DATE
    `but before`              IS A DATE
    `amount`                  IS A NUMBER

`the s 18D to 18M periods` MEANS
    LIST `Grant period` OF "s 18(2)(ad), s 18D", YMD 2016 7 1, YMD 2017 7 1, 20000
         `Grant period` OF "s 18(2)(ae), s 18E", YMD 2017 7 1, YMD 2018 7 1, 20000
         `Grant period` OF "s 18(2)(af), s 18F", YMD 2018 7 1, YMD 2019 7 1, 20000
         `Grant period` OF "s 18(2)(ag), s 18G", YMD 2019 7 1, YMD 2020 7 1, 20000
         `Grant period` OF "s 18(2)(ah), s 18H", YMD 2020 7 1, YMD 2021 4 1, 20000
         `Grant period` OF "s 18(2)(ai), s 18I", YMD 2021 4 1, YMD 2022 7 1, 30000
         `Grant period` OF "s 18(2)(aj), s 18J", YMD 2022 7 1, YMD 2023 7 1, 30000
         `Grant period` OF "s 18(2)(ak), s 18K", YMD 2023 7 1, YMD 2024 7 1, 30000
         `Grant period` OF "s 18(2)(al), s 18L", YMD 2025 7 1, YMD 2026 7 1, 30000
         `Grant period` OF "s 18(2)(am), s 18M", YMD 2026 7 1, YMD 2027 7 1, 20000

`the months allowed to complete (ss 18D-18M)` MEANS 24
`the day s 18 was substituted` MEANS YMD 2013 1 1
`the first day after the s 18A to 18C periods` MEANS YMD 2016 1 1
`the day the $10 000 amount starts (s 18(2)(b)(ii))` MEANS YMD 2015 7 1

DECLARE `Grant amount answer` IS ONE OF
    `the grant, in dollars, is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER, `under` IS A STRING
    `not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

GIVEN `t` IS A `Grant transaction`
      `p` IS A `Grant period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `satisfies the period` IF
        (`t`'s `the commencement date` `is on or after` (`p`'s `commencing on or after`))
    AND (`t`'s `the commencement date` `is before` (`p`'s `but before`))
    AND (    (`t`'s `the completion date` `is on or before` (`the day that is` `the months allowed to complete (ss 18D-18M)` `months after` (`t`'s `the commencement date`)))
         OR `t`'s `the Commissioner extended the time for completion (ss 18D(3)-18M(2))`)
    AND (NOT `t`'s `the Commissioner considers it replaces an earlier transaction between substantially the same parties (ss 18D(4)-18M(3))`)

GIVEN `t` IS A `Grant transaction`
      `periods` IS A LIST OF `Grant period`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Grant period`
`the period satisfied by` `t` `among` `periods` MEANS
    CONSIDER `periods`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `p` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN
        IF `satisfies the period` `t` `p`
        THEN JUST `p`
        ELSE `the period satisfied by` `t` `among` `rest`

GIVEN `t` IS A `Grant transaction`
GIVETH A `Grant amount answer`
`the s 18 amount for` MEANS
    IF `t`'s `the commencement date` `is before` `the day s 18 was substituted`
    THEN `not covered` `the grant's commencement date is before 1 January 2013, when s 18 was substituted (No. 3 of 2013); the amount in force before then is not in the deposited consolidation`
    ELSE IF     `t`'s `the commencement date` `is before` `the first day after the s 18A to 18C periods`
            AND `the transaction is for a new home`
         THEN `not covered` `the commencement date falls in a s 18A, 18B or 18C period (1 January 2013 to 31 December 2015) and the transaction is for a new home: those sections' building-commencement conditions are not encoded`
         ELSE CONSIDER `the period satisfied by` `t` `among` `the s 18D to 18M periods`
              WHEN JUST `p` THEN `the grant, in dollars, is` (`the lesser of` (`t`'s `the consideration`) (`p`'s `amount`)) (`p`'s `section`)
              WHEN NOTHING THEN
                  IF `t`'s `the commencement date` `is before` `the day the $10 000 amount starts (s 18(2)(b)(ii))`
                  THEN `the grant, in dollars, is` (`the lesser of` (`t`'s `the consideration`) 7000) "s 18(2)(b)(i)"
                  ELSE `the grant, in dollars, is` (`the lesser of` (`t`'s `the consideration`) 10000) "s 18(2)(b)(ii)"
    WHERE
        -- READING (finding 19): ss 18A(2), 18B(2) and 18C(2) say "An eligible transaction satisfies this section if --
        -- (a) the commencement date ... is on or after [from] but before [to]; and (b) where the eligible transaction is
        -- -- (i) a comprehensive home building contract for a new home ...; (ii) the building of a new home by an owner
        -- builder ...; (iii) a contract for an off-the-plan purchase of a new home ...; or (iv) a contract for the
        -- purchase of a new home, the eligible transaction is completed in accordance with section 13(5)." Every kind
        -- (b) names is a new home. Read as a list of the kinds that can satisfy the section, (b) leaves out a contract
        -- for an established home (possible only before 1 July 2014, s 13(1)(a)), which then takes s 18(2)(b)(i),
        -- $7 000. That is the reading taken. Item (iv) supports it: it adds nothing but completion, which s 7(1)(b)(ii)
        -- requires anyway, so it is there to name a kind, not to add a condition. The words also bear the other
        -- reading: that "where the eligible transaction is" sets conditions only for the kinds it names, so that an
        -- established-home contract meets the section on (a) alone and takes $15 000 (s 18A), $30 000 (s 18B) or
        -- $20 000 (s 18C). That reading is not taken.
        `the transaction is for a new home` MEANS
            CONSIDER `t`'s `kind`
            WHEN `a contract to buy a home` THEN `is a new home (FHOG Act s 3)` (`t`'s `the home`)
            OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `s 14(5)-(6) -- the application period`

-- s 14(5): "An application may only be made within a period (the "application period") -- (a) commencing on the
-- commencement date of the eligible transaction to which the application relates; and (b) ending 12 months after the
-- completion of the eligible transaction". (6): "However, the Commissioner has a discretion to allow an application before
-- or after the application period."
`the months after completion to apply (s 14(5)(b))` MEANS 12

GIVEN `t` IS A `Grant transaction`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the application period for` MEANS
    `the day that is` `the months after completion to apply (s 14(5)(b))` `months after` (`t`'s `the completion date`)

DECLARE `Application timing answer` IS ONE OF
    `within the application period, which ends on` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `outside the application period, but the Commissioner has allowed it (s 14(6))`
    `outside the application period: only if the Commissioner allows it (s 14(6))` HAS `the period ran from` IS A DATE, `to` IS A DATE

-- The Commissioner's s 14(6) discretion is an input: whether the Commissioner has allowed the application.
GIVEN `t` IS A `Grant transaction`
      `the day of the application` IS A DATE
      `the Commissioner has allowed it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Application timing answer`
`the s 14(5) timing of` `t` `the day of the application` `the Commissioner has allowed it` MEANS
    IF `the day falls from` `the day of the application` `to` (`t`'s `the commencement date`) `and` (`the last day of the application period for` `t`)
    THEN `within the application period, which ends on` (`the last day of the application period for` `t`)
    ELSE IF `the Commissioner has allowed it`
         THEN `outside the application period, but the Commissioner has allowed it (s 14(6))`
         ELSE `outside the application period: only if the Commissioner allows it (s 14(6))` (`t`'s `the commencement date`) (`the last day of the application period for` `t`)

-- The same as a permission: the applicant may apply within the period; not applying is no breach. Clock: the
-- commencement date.
GIVEN `t` IS A `Grant transaction`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Duty act`
`s 14(5) -- the applicant may apply for the grant within the application period` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant for the grant`
    MAY   `apply for the grant`
    WITHIN `the days from` (`t`'s `the commencement date`) `until` (`the last day of the application period for` `t`)

§§ `s 19(3) -- the grant applied to State taxes`

-- s 19(3): "If the applicant requests, the Commissioner may apply the amount of a first home owner grant, or part of the
-- amount, towards a liability for State taxes, fees or charges." So the grant can pay the transfer duty: what is left.
GIVEN `the duty` IS A NUMBER, `the grant` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the duty left after the grant is applied (s 19(3))` MEANS
    `the greater of` 0 (`the duty` MINUS `the grant`)

GIVEN `the duty` IS A NUMBER, `the grant` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the grant left over after paying the duty (s 19(3))` MEANS
    `the greater of` 0 (`the grant` MINUS `the duty`)

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Duty act`
`s 19(3) -- on request, the Commissioner may apply the grant towards the duty` MEANS
    PARTY `the Commissioner`
    MAY   `apply the grant towards a liability for State taxes`

§§ `s 20 -- a grant paid in anticipation of the residence requirement (regulative)`

-- s 20(1): the Commissioner may pay in anticipation if satisfied each applicant who has not yet complied intends to.
-- (2)-(3): if the requirement is not complied with, notice and repayment "within 14 days after the relevant date", which
-- is "the earlier of the following: (a) the end of the period allowed for compliance with the residence requirement; (b)
-- the date on which it first becomes apparent that the residence requirement will not be complied with during the period
-- allowed for compliance." (3A): the same within 14 days after ceasing to retain the relevant interest, "unless the
-- Commissioner has exempted the applicant from the residence requirement in accordance with section 12(2)".
-- The trace form: the residence requirement in tda-common.l4, clock starting at completion.
GIVEN `the Commissioner exempted this joint applicant (s 12(2))` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the completion date`                                    IS A DATE
      `the months allowed to begin occupying`                  IS A NUMBER
      `the months of occupation required`                      IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Duty act`
`ss 12, 20 -- the applicant's residence requirement after a grant paid in anticipation` `the Commissioner exempted this joint applicant (s 12(2))` `the completion date` `the months allowed to begin occupying` `the months of occupation required` MEANS
    `the residence requirement under` `a first home owner grant paid in anticipation (FHOG Act ss 12, 20)` `the Commissioner exempted this joint applicant (s 12(2))` (DATE_SERIAL `the completion date`) (DATE_SERIAL (`the day that is` `the months allowed to begin occupying` `months after` `the completion date`)) `the months of occupation required`

-- s 20(3)(a): the end of the period allowed for compliance. READING: the period ends when a continuous 6 months that
-- began on the last day to begin would end -- that is, the last day to begin plus the months of occupation.
GIVEN `the completion date`                   IS A DATE
      `the months allowed to begin occupying` IS A NUMBER
      `the months of occupation required`     IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the end of the period allowed for compliance (s 20(3)(a))` MEANS
    `the day that is` `the months of occupation required` `months after` (`the day that is` `the months allowed to begin occupying` `months after` `the completion date`)

-- s 20(3): the relevant date, the earlier of (a) and (b).
GIVEN `the end of the period allowed for compliance`    IS A DATE
      `the day it first became apparent`              IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the relevant date (s 20(3))` MEANS
    IF `the day it first became apparent` `is before` `the end of the period allowed for compliance`
    THEN `the day it first became apparent`
    ELSE `the end of the period allowed for compliance`

-- The situation form: once the relevant date has come (or the interest has been given up), the clock starts on that day
-- and the applicant must give notice and repay within 14 days.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Duty act`
`s 20(2), (3A) -- after the relevant date, give notice and repay within 14 days` MEANS
    `what follows a failure under` `a first home owner grant paid in anticipation (FHOG Act ss 12, 20)`

-- s 20(3A): "If a first home owner grant is paid in anticipation of compliance with the residence requirement and an
-- applicant ceases to retain his or her relevant interest in the land before satisfying the residence requirement,
-- the applicant must, within 14 days after ceasing to retain his or her relevant interest -- (a) give written notice
-- of that fact to the Commissioner; and (b) repay the amount of the grant -- unless the Commissioner has exempted the
-- applicant from the residence requirement in accordance with section 12(2)." The last day, or nothing to do.
DECLARE `Interest given up answer` IS ONE OF
    `the applicant must give the Commissioner written notice and repay the grant no later than` HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `nothing: the Commissioner exempted the applicant from the residence requirement (s 12(2))`

GIVEN `the Commissioner exempted the applicant (s 12(2))` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the applicant ceased to retain the interest` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Interest given up answer`
`s 20(3A) -- what the applicant must do after ceasing to retain the interest` `the Commissioner exempted the applicant (s 12(2))` `the day the applicant ceased to retain the interest` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner exempted the applicant (s 12(2))`
    THEN `nothing: the Commissioner exempted the applicant from the residence requirement (s 12(2))`
    ELSE `the applicant must give the Commissioner written notice and repay the grant no later than` (`the day that is` `the days to act after a failure of the residence requirement` `days after` `the day the applicant ceased to retain the interest`)

§§ `s 38 -- a written notice to repay (regulative)`

-- s 38(1): "The Commissioner may, by written notice, require an applicant (or former applicant) ... to repay an amount
-- paid on the application if -- (a) the amount was paid in error; or (b) the Commissioner varies or reverses the decision
-- under which the amount was paid in accordance with section 23." (3): "If an applicant ... fails to make a repayment
-- required under this section or the conditions of the grant, the Commissioner may, by written notice, impose a penalty
-- not exceeding the amount the applicant ... is required to repay." s 39(2): joint applicants are jointly and severally
-- liable; s 39(4A): the time to pay is the time "specified in the notice under section 38". s 21(3): compliance by one
-- joint applicant is compliance by all. Clock: the day of the notice.
GIVEN `the days the notice allows` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Duty act`
`s 38 -- repay within the time the notice allows, or the Commissioner may impose a penalty` `the days the notice allows` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant for the grant`
    MUST  `repay the grant`
    WITHIN `the days the notice allows`
    LEST
        PARTY `the Commissioner`
        MAY   `impose a penalty not exceeding the amount to be repaid`

-- s 38(3): the most the penalty can be.
GIVEN `the amount to be repaid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most penalty that can be imposed (s 38(3))` MEANS
    `the amount to be repaid`
